# Floor beam B1

Simply supported beam, uniformly loaded, laterally restrained by the slab.
Profile IPE 300, steel S355.

## Geometry and loads

```math
L    = 6.0 m        # span
q_Ed = 25 kN/m      # design load, ULS 6.10b
q_ser = 18 kN/m     # characteristic load, SLS
```

```math
M_Ed = q_Ed * L^2 / 8
V_Ed = q_Ed * L / 2
```

## Section and material

IPE 300, values from the profile table.

```math
h   = 300 mm
b   = 150 mm
t_w = 7.1 mm
t_f = 10.7 mm
r   = 15 mm
A   = 5381 mm^2
A_v = 2568 mm^2       # shear area, z-z
I_y = 8356e4 mm^4
W_el_y = 557.1e3 mm^3
W_pl_y = 628.4e3 mm^3

f_y = 355 MPa
E   = 210 GPa
gamma_M0 = 1.0
gamma_M1 = 1.0
```

## Classification

Outstand flange in compression, Table 5.2.

```math
eps = sqrt(235 MPa / f_y)
c_f = (b - t_w - 2 r) / 2
c_f / t_f

if c_f / t_f <= 9 eps
  cls = 1
else if c_f / t_f <= 10 eps
  cls = 2
else
  cls = 3
end
```

The flange is class {cls}, so the plastic section modulus is used.

## Bending resistance, 6.2.5

```math
M_c_Rd = W_pl_y * f_y / gamma_M0 to kNm      # (6.13)
check M_Ed <= M_c_Rd
```

## Shear resistance, 6.2.6

```math
V_pl_Rd = A_v * f_y / sqrt(3) / gamma_M0 to kN   # (6.18)
check V_Ed <= V_pl_Rd
check V_Ed <= 0.5 V_pl_Rd   # no M-V interaction, 6.2.8(2)
```

## Deflection

Limit L/250 for the characteristic combination.

```math
delta     = 5 q_ser L^4 / (384 E I_y) to mm
delta_lim = L / 250 to mm
check delta <= delta_lim
```

## Summary

Bending utilization {M_Ed / M_c_Rd}, shear {V_Ed / V_pl_Rd}, deflection {delta / delta_lim}.
IPE 300 S355 is adequate.
